course: dictionary
lesson: 11461
title: Adolescence: the time of growing up
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Adolescence is a noun. It means the time of life between being a child and being an adult, roughly the teenage years. «During adolescence, many young people grow taller and their voices change.» The sentence tells you what happens in this time: children are growing into adults.
explain: You may also meet adolescence in a second sense, about something young that is still growing. «The club is in its adolescence and has only ten members.» Here adolescence means an early stage of growth, like a young club, country or idea. Look for clues: is the thing still young and developing?
explain: Adolescence often appears in small phrases: «in adolescence», «during adolescence», «early adolescence». Early adolescence means the first part of those years. To check your meaning, swap in "the teenage years" or "the time of growing up". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Adolescence is a noun, so it names a time or a stage.
fact: «Adolescence» means the time between being a child and being an adult, roughly the teenage years.
fact: «Adolescence» can also mean an early stage of growth, like a young country or idea.
fact: Useful phrases: «in adolescence», «during adolescence», «early adolescence».
exercise: «My brother is in adolescence now, and he is fourteen.» What does adolescence mean here? | A kind of cold weather | *The time between childhood and adulthood | A tiny shop | A long school holiday
exercise: «The new club is still in its adolescence and has only ten members.» What does adolescence mean here? | A yearly party | The very end of a long life | *An early stage of growth
exercise: Which word best completes this sentence? «Adolescence is the time between being a ___ and being an adult.» | window | bridge | puddle | *child
test: «My cousin says her adolescence was the hardest and best time of her life.» What does adolescence mean here? | A school trip | A kind of medicine | *The teenage years, between childhood and adulthood | A type of weather
test: «Early adolescence can bring new feelings and new friends.» What does early adolescence mean? | *The first part of the time between childhood and adulthood | A time before a child is born | Very old age | A kind of cloud
exam: Which sentence uses adolescence with its correct meaning? | *«Her adolescence began when she started secondary school.» | «The adolescence of the bus was cold and wet.» | «He ate a big adolescence for tea.» | «We sat under the adolescence on the sunny beach.»
